{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-business-accounts-compliance-guidelines-reporting-to-adyen","reason":"The pinned raw matches the trusted SHA-256, all five quotes match their line locators, and the dated event, daily-fraud and quarterly-complaint timing and routes are supported. The UK/Ireland summary can misanswer what goes in the quarterly report: raw lines 94-100 say complaint reporting must contain the three table data points (total vulnerable users, totals broken down by vulnerability category, and outcomes of additional-support requests), while line 104 says only total figures for vulnerable users are required. The candidate and Q2 query answer present category and outcome details as CRM records and the report as only totals without preserving the table's reporting requirement or its tension with line 104. The related financial-products source and reciprocal Business Accounts route are relevant."}
